 "head_interlock": {
  "_note": "JOINT_LIMITS.md section 2: roll only while abs(head yaw) <= yaw_window_deg, then abs(roll) <= roll_max_deg; yaw only while abs(roll) <= roll_free_deg. yaw_window_deg and roll_free_deg are the design's (tools/import_design.py): at +-1.0 deg of yaw the head base clears the head-pitch U by 0.31 mm or more at every roll; the independent review had found it cutting 0.16-0.40 mm into the U at yaw -2 to -2.5 with roll -10 to -15, inside the window of that time (2.5). The two margins are the firmware's own and are subtracted: roll stops at 15 - 2 = 13 deg, a placeholder until the head is seen moving on the bench.",
  "yaw_window_deg": 1.0,
  "yaw_margin_deg": 0.0,
  "roll_max_deg": 15.0,
  "roll_margin_deg": 2.0,
  "roll_free_deg": 1.0
 },
